        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "“Dun An Oir” – A Rare Opportunity to Own a Truly Special Home in Howth\r\n\r\nSet on a glorious elevated site of approximately two-thirds of an acre, Dun An Oir presents a rare opportunity for a family to acquire a remarkable detached residence in one of Howth’s most scenic and sought-after locations. This spacious two-storey home, extending to c. 2,665 sq. ft., is beautifully complemented by a purpose-built studio (c. 375 sq. ft.) and a garage with adjoining workshop (c. 475 sq. ft.), offering superb flexibility for modern family living, working from home, or hosting guests.\r\n\r\nFrom the moment you arrive, the setting is breathtaking. Perched above Carrickbrack Road, the property enjoys a commanding position with panoramic views that stretch nearly 180 degrees—from the east of Dublin Bay, across the city skyline, and all the way westward towards Dublin Airport. By day, the views are simply stunning; by night, the city lights provide a magical, ever-changing backdrop.\r\n\r\nInside, the accommodation is bright and generously proportioned, offering great potential for those who wish to modernise or reimagine this cherished home. The layout includes a welcoming reception hall, three reception rooms, a well-sized kitchen, four bedrooms, and two bathrooms.\r\nOutside, the mature gardens are a true delight—lush green lawns, planted borders, and tall pines provide privacy and tranquility in equal measure. The detached studio, positioned to the rear and elevated for maximum light and views, is a hidden gem, ideal as a creative workspace, home office, or charming guest retreat.\r\n\r\nThis part of the Howth-Sutton peninsula is celebrated for its uniquely mild microclimate, scenic coastal walks, and unrivalled views. Though it enjoys a peaceful, rural atmosphere, Dun An Oir is just minutes from the vibrant communities of Sutton Cross and Howth Village. Excellent transport links, including regular bus routes and nearby DART stations, place the city centre and Dublin Airport within easy reach.\r\n\r\nWhether you're seeking a comfortable family home with scope to grow, or the perfect canvas to create a contemporary masterpiece (subject to planning), Dun An Oir is a property that must be seen to be fully appreciated.\r\n\r\nTo arrange a private viewing, please contact us at info@gallagherquigley.ie or call +353 1 818 3000."
      },
